  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Idaho totaled $3.3B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Energy is the largest buyer, obligating $2.5B, followed by the Department of Agriculture at $437M and the Department of Defense at $177M. Contractors won 9,024 awards at an average award size of $371K. Obligations fell 15.1% year over year. Battelle Energy Alliance, LLC received the largest vendor total at $2B, and Idaho Environmental Coalition LLC received $526M. The largest industry by NAICS was All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $2B, with Remediation Services at $533M and Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $236M. Fiscal-year trends show variability: obligations were $2.8B in FY21, $2.5B in FY22, $3.2B in FY23, $3.8B in FY24, $3.9B in FY25, and $3.3B in FY26 to date. These figures are contract obligations and FY2026 totals are partial, covering the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What agencies are the largest buyers in Idaho?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy leads buying with $2.5B in obligations. The Department of Agriculture follows with $437M, then the Department of Defense with $177M. Smaller federal buyers include the Department of the Interior at $126M and the Department of Transportation at $27.2M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries capture the most federal dollars in Idaho?",
        "body": "Battelle Energy Alliance, LLC is the top vendor with $2B in obligations, and Idaho Environmental Coalition LLC is second with $526M. The largest industry is All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $2B, with Remediation Services at $533M and Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $236M."
      }
    ]
